A loop that wraps its own error builds an unbounded chain: with -chain-depth=3 the deepest entry is marked [chain truncated], and the run terminates.
-- args --
-chain-depth=3 a.go:@f
-- stdout --
$WORK/a.go:10:12-13: Error Set of example.com/fx.F: 5 entries
$WORK/a.go:8:5-9: sentinel example.com/fx.ErrX
	path (origin → target):
		$WORK/a.go:11:9-13: in example.com/fx.F
$WORK/a.go:8:5-9: sentinel example.com/fx.ErrX
	wrap chain (origin → target):
		$WORK/a.go:13:9-42: fmt.Errorf "step %d: %w"
	path (origin → target):
		$WORK/a.go:11:9-13: in example.com/fx.F
$WORK/a.go:8:5-9: sentinel example.com/fx.ErrX
	wrap chain (origin → target):
